{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed the silent-failure bug and documented both causes in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n- Claude was not authenticated under launchd, so no review was generated.\n- `status` is read-only in zsh; assigning `$?` to it crashed the script before notification. Replaced it with `exit_code` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh:19`.\n\nVerified with local mocks that both failure notifications and successful summaries are sent. Shell syntax and plist validation pass. No external services were contacted.\n\nSuccessful reviews still require a one-time interactive Claude login as the `vk` user (`claude`, then `/login`). Until then, the job will now send a failure note instead of staying silent."}
